<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">69.13</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">79.97</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">77.62</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">65.32</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">62.67</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">61.33</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">62.46</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">59.42</span></td>
<td id="Sx3.T1.1.10.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx3.T1.1.10.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">61.49</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>t-MAP@5000 of different targeted adversarial attack methods with 16,32 and 64 hash bits on three datasets. The best results are highlighted in bold, while the second-best results are underlined.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx3.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Optimization and Reconstruction</h3>

<div id="Sx3.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During denoising iterations, attention maps are aggregated to analyze the model’s focus on image regions relevant to the original text. By leveraging textual guidance derived from the original image, we constrain deviations in attention distribution through variance minimization. This approach ensures semantic coherence and maintains consistent attention to textually relevant regions throughout the optimization process. This is mathematically represented as:</p>
<table id="Sx3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attention}}=\frac{1}{H\times W\times S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{w=1}^{W}\left(\mathcal{A}_{h,w}^{s}(z_{Bt})-\mu_{s}\right)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Attention</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attention}}=\frac{1}{H\times W\times S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{w=1}^{W}\left(\mathcal{A}_{h,w}^{s}(z_{Bt})-\mu_{s}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{h,w}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{h,w}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the attention value at location <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,w)</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-th attention head, <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of attention heads, <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are the spatial dimensions of the attention map, <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean attention value for the <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-th attention head. <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Bt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bt}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the latent benign text vector, which provides semantic guidance to the attention mechanism.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx3.SSx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.SSx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure perceptual quality while achieving the adversarial objective, we add reconstruction loss to guide the optimization. It enforces latent-level consistency, promote smoothness preserving both low-level details and high-level features between the original and adversarial images. This is mathematically represented as:</p>
<table id="Sx3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Recon}}=\frac{1}{H_{z}\times W_{z}}\sum_{i=1}^{H_{z}}\sum_{j=1}^{W_{z}}[\bigl(z_{Bi}^{0}(i,j)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}\\[-2.0pt]
+\bigl(z_{Bi}^{t}(i+1,j)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}+\bigl(z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j+1)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Recon</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msup><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Recon}}=\frac{1}{H_{z}\times W_{z}}\sum_{i=1}^{H_{z}}\sum_{j=1}^{W_{z}}[\bigl(z_{Bi}^{0}(i,j)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}\\[-2.0pt]
+\bigl(z_{Bi}^{t}(i+1,j)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}+\bigl(z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j+1)-z_{Bi}^{t}(i,j)\bigr)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx3.SSx4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the height and width of the latent vector, while <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,H_{z}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,H_{z}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,W_{z}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,W_{z}\}</annotation></semantics></math> index its spatial coordinates. The <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Bi}^{0}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bi}^{0}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the latent value at location <math id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> for the original image. Finally, our whole optimization goal could be defined as:</p>
<table id="Sx3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="argmin\quad\kappa_{1}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Attack}+\kappa_{2}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Recon}+\kappa_{3}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Attention}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">argmin\quad\kappa_{1}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Attack}+\kappa_{2}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Recon}+\kappa_{3}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{Attention}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx3.SSx4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The outline of DiffHash is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Optimization and Reconstruction ‣ Method ‣ DiffHash: Text-Guided Targeted Attack via Diffusion Models against Deep Hashing Image Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> DiffHash Targeted Attack</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Clean query image <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, latent benign text <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Bt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bt}</annotation></semantics></math>, target image <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, latent target text <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Tt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Tt}</annotation></semantics></math>, Diffusion model <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Deep hashing model <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, HashAlignNet <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{HAN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>HAN</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{HAN}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Loss weights: <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2},\kappa_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{1},\kappa_{2},\kappa_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, Total inversion steps <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> , learning rate <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output</span>: Adversarial image <math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
             Obtain latent representation from <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Bi}^{0}=Inverse(x_{i}^{t-1})=Inverse\circ\ldots\circ Inverse(x_{i}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bi}^{0}=Inverse(x_{i}^{t-1})=Inverse\circ\ldots\circ Inverse(x_{i}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(T_{F},b_{t}\bigr)\;\leftarrow\;f_{\mathrm{HAN}}(z_{Tt})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>HAN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(T_{F},b_{t}\bigr)\;\leftarrow\;f_{\mathrm{HAN}}(z_{Tt})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(I_{F},b_{Bt}\bigr)\;\leftarrow\;f_{\mathrm{HAN}}(z_{Bt})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>HAN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(I_{F},b_{Bt}\bigr)\;\leftarrow\;f_{\mathrm{HAN}}(z_{Bt})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
             <span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{Bi}^{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{diffusion\_step}\bigl(\mathcal{M},\;z_{Bi}^{t-1},\;z_{Bt},\;t\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>diffusion</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>step</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bi}^{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{diffusion\_step}\bigl(\mathcal{M},\;z_{Bi}^{t-1},\;z_{Bt},\;t\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\min\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Total}}=\kappa_{1}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attack}}(b_{t},b(z_{Bi}^{t}))+\kappa_{2}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Recon}}(z_{Bi}^{0},z_{Bi}^{t})+\kappa_{3}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attention}}(z_{Bt})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Total</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Attack</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Recon</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Attention</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\min\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Total}}=\kappa_{1}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attack}}(b_{t},b(z_{Bi}^{t}))+\kappa_{2}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Recon}}(z_{Bi}^{0},z_{Bi}^{t})+\kappa_{3}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Attention}}(z_{Bt}).</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(z_{Bi}^{t})=f_{\text{HAN}}(z_{Bi}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>HAN</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(z_{Bi}^{t})=f_{\text{HAN}}(z_{Bi}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{Bi}^{t}\;\longleftarrow\;z_{Bi}^{t}-\eta\,\nabla\bigl(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Total}}(z_{Bi}^{t},z_{Bt},z_{Bi}^{0})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⟵</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em">∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Total</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{Bi}^{t}\;\longleftarrow\;z_{Bi}^{t}-\eta\,\nabla\bigl(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Total}}(z_{Bi}^{t},z_{Bt},z_{Bi}^{0})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
             <span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\;\leftarrow\;{\mathrm{Decode}}(\mathcal{M},z_{Bi}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Decode</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\;\leftarrow\;{\mathrm{Decode}}(\mathcal{M},z_{Bi}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
             <span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Adversarial image <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Experiment</h2>

<section id="Sx4.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Experiment Setup and Preparation</h3>

<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, we evaluate our method on three multi-label datasets: FLICKR-25K (38 labels, 1,900 query/target images)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huiskes and Lew 2008</a>)</cite>, NUS-WIDE (21 labels, 2,100 query/target images)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chua et al. 2009</a>)</cite>, and MS-COCO (80 labels, 1,800 query/target images) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. 2014</a>)</cite>, each with 5,000 images randomly selected for hash alignment. For consistency, we use an LLM (e.g., Fuyu-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">AI 2023</a>)</cite> using the prompt: <span id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write a simple five-sentence description of this image.</span> to generate five descriptions per image, filtering out descriptions with low CLIP similarity (<math id="Sx4.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> 0.25) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al. 2021</a>)</cite>. We evaluate targeted attack effectiveness using target mean average precision (t-MAP) on the top 5,000 retrieved images from the database following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. 2023</a>)</cite>. Higher t-MAP scores indicate better attack performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, we use CSQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al. 2020</a>)</cite> with a ResNet-50 backbone as the baseline hashing model. We compare our DiffHash against SOTA targeted attack methods: P2P <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al. 2020</a>)</cite>, DHTA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al. 2020</a>)</cite>, PTA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, Pros-Gan <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2021b</a>)</cite>, THA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2021a</a>)</cite>, and HUANG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang and Shen 2025</a>)</cite> , with perturbation constraint <math id="Sx4.SSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=8/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=8/255</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation Details.</span> We employ pre-trained <span id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Stable Diffusion v2-base</span> with DDIM sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song, Meng, and Ermon 2021</a>)</cite>. Optimization uses AdamW (<math id="Sx4.SSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lr=1e^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lr=1e^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, 30 iterations) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov 2017</a>)</cite>. Experiments are conducted on an NVIDIA RTX 4090D GPU, where DiffHash generates adversarial examples with 16.59 GB of GPU memory.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Sx4.T2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="Sx4.T2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="Sx4.T2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Method</span></th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="Sx4.T2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Metric</span></th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">NUS-WIDE</th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">FLICKR-25K</th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">MS-COCO</th></tr>
<tr id="Sx4.T2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx4.T2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPH</span></th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx4.T2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HashNet</span></th>
<th id="Sx4.T2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="Sx4.T2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPSH</span></th>
